        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "NOTE The parameters related to current, power and voltage provided in Schedule Exchange message pair can be considered as physical limitations, meaning that they are related to the physical abilities of the system under rated operating conditions. Later during the energy transfer process, depending on the external and environmental conditions (State of Charge (SOC), temperatures, etc.), the values of these limitations can change into more conservative values.",
